# COSMOS .gitignore - DENY BY DEFAULT, and that is deliberate.
#
# 🔴 THE PREDECESSOR DID THE OPPOSITE AND DOCUMENTED WHY IT WAS DANGEROUS.
# bts-mesh ships everything - "private repo, push it all there" - and its own .gitignore carries
# the warning: "THE ONE THING THAT WOULD MAKE THIS WRONG IS THE REPO GOING PUBLIC. If it is ever
# flipped, the credentials in gemini_cli_env.json and every balance in the ledgers go with it.
# That is a property of the REPO, not of this file."
#
# COSMOS IS BUILT TO BE DISTRIBUTED - Jack, Grayson, a cold machine. So the exposure question is
# settled at commit one instead of at publish time: CODE AND GOVERNANCE IN, STATE AND SECRETS OUT.
# => A repo that never contained a secret needs no scrub, no history rewrite, and no decision on
#    the day someone flips it public. A CLEAN REPO IS CHEAPER THAN A CLEANED ONE.

# ---- SECRETS. Never, under any name, on any branch. ----
.secrets/
*_key.txt
*_token.txt
*api_key*
*apikey*
*_env.json
gemini_cli_env.json
credentials*.json
*.pem

# ---- LIVE STATE. Belongs to a running instance, not to the software. ----
# Shipping these is how a peer install inherits somebody else's history and believes it.
live/
*.lock
*_ledger.jsonl
*_heartbeat*.json
*_state/
*_state.json
mesh_state.json
dash.json
bench.json
chan.json
drive_health.json
spend*.json
*_spend*.json
budget_knobs.json

# ---- QUEUE AND RUNTIME OUTPUT ----
_queue/
_lanes/
_delme/
tmp/
logs/
*.log
out/

# ---- PYTHON ----
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/

# ---- EDITOR / OS ----
.vscode/
.idea/
~$*
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# ---- BACKUPS AND STAGED DELETIONS ----
*.bak
*.bak-*
delme__*
*.PRE_*
